  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "One ECS for the demo",
      "items": [
        "web and worker share one image; only the start command differs",
        "Pick one database: A = RDS (automatic backup) or B = db container on the ECS (cheaper, back up yourself)",
        "COMPOSE_PROFILES in .env picks the extra containers: ocr for A, localdb,ocr for B",
        "Images come from Docker Hub (quix07); files live on the app_data volume (back up with EVS snapshots)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Network rules",
      "items": [
        "Only 80/443 are open on the ECS (22 for the team IP); web login is off unless BASIC_AUTH_HASH is set",
        "RDS has no public IP and accepts 5432 from the ECS group only",
        "All outbound calls leave through the ECS EIP, so no NAT gateway"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Still to check",
      "items": [
        "pgvector on RDS in AP-Bangkok (without it the app falls back to numpy, or use option B)",
        "Whether the advisor's LLM endpoint accepts Huawei Cloud IPs",
        "Steps 1-9 in DEPLOY.md cover both options"
      ]
    }
  ]
